You are wrong, as usual.

Save scumming is backing up save files to guard against _in-game_
blunders. What Chris is doing is using one in case of _external_
disaster, which is a different thing altogether. It is usually not
necessary any more on most systems, but it is no less ethical than using
the normal recovery system which is built into most versions of NetHack
nowadays.
I.o.w., if you use your backup file to circumvent your own cockups, that
is not cricket. Chris is hoping to circumvent a cockup on the part of
the power company, and that is fine.

